Translation patch: binlog functions restructured around Aeneas' borrow/join limitations

Change: Code after a join that runs while a borrowed `self` containing borrows (or a `ParseBuf`) is live moves into helpers that get the needed values or fields, in tail position: `Event::len`/`checksum` (free fns `event_len`/`event_checksum` on copied fields), `FormatDescriptionEvent::get_event_type_header_length` (the default-length `match` in `default_event_type_header_length`, computed before the lookup), `RowsEvent::len`/`serialize`/`deserialize` (`rows_event_len`, `serialize_extra_data`, `serialize_bitmap`, `deserialize_rows_event`, which receives the two post-header lengths read from the FDE up front), `UserVarEvent::len` (`user_var_event_len`), `TableMapEvent::json_column_count`/`get_column_metadata`/`get_real_type`/`len` (`count_json_columns`, `column_metadata_from`, `real_string_type`; `columns_count()` read first), `PreviousGtidsEvent` (`n_sids_of_header`, `parse_sid_tag`, `any_tagged`, `header_of_n_sids`, `serialize_sids`/`serialize_sid`/`serialize_sid_tag`/`serialize_intervals` as recursion over slices), `GtidEvent::serialize_untagged`/`len_untagged` (on a struct `LogicalClockFields` of the copied fields), `TransactionPayloadEvent::serialize` (`serialize_uncompressed_size`), `BinlogRow::unwrap` (recursive `unwrap_values` with `Vec::pop` and `panic!` with the `expect` message).
Why: Aeneas fails to join contexts after a conditional when the borrowed `self` contains borrows ("Could not match the contexts"), and fails ("Unreachable") on a method call on `self` while a borrow of a field containing borrows is live (cf. patches 17, 29, 30); loops over `&[T]` where `T` holds borrows and closures are not supported.
Behaviour: Identical: every value read up front is a pure read of the event or of the format description event (the reads cannot panic), the helpers contain the moved statements unchanged, and the recursions perform the loops' iterations in order. `unwrap_values` panics (with the same message) exactly when some value is `None`.

